			<script type="application/json" data-sveltekit-fetched data-url="https://query1.finance.yahoo.com/ws/company-fundamentals/v1/finance/price-insights?aiModules=news_summary&amp;modules=ai&amp;symbols=AAPL&amp;checkAnomaly=false&amp;lang=en-US&amp;region=US" data-hash="1hxquyi" data-ttl="1">{"status":200,"statusText":"","headers":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=1, stale-while-revalidate=9"},"body":"{\"finance\":{\"result\":{\"AAPL\":{\"aiAnalysis\":{\"rank\":2,\"data\":{\"price_movement\":{\"data\":{\"recent_news_articles\":[{\"title\":\"State Street SPDR Portfolio S&P 500 (SPYM) Buys $75.6 Million More Apple on Monday\",\"summary\":\"On Nov. 9, 2026 State Street SPDR Portfolio S&P 500 ETF (SPYM) was the biggest net buyer among funds, adding $960.4 million of stock with no sales and increasing 502 of 503 positions; the fund’s assets stood at $183.21 billion. Its largest purchases were Apple ($75.6M, 215,481 shares, 7.87% of the fund), NVIDIA ($63.9M, 357,399 shares, 6.64%), Microsoft ($59.7M, 109,585 shares, 6.22%), Amazon ($38.7M, 144,956 shares, 4.03%) and Alphabet A ($24.9M, 86,583 shares, 2.6%). SPYM is an Equity US ETF with 503 holdings, 37.4% in its top 10, heavy on Technology (36.9%), charges a 0.02% expense ratio, and lists metrics including a GF Score of 88, P/E 23.22, P/B 4.74, dividend yield 1.08% and year-to-date return +10.92%. Investors should watch for any future rebalancing or changes in weights for Apple, NVIDIA and Microsoft.\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/state-street-spdr-portfolio-p-110320237.html\",\"article_id\":\"a612223c-75f9-3325-babd-1f086b72d615\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:03:20Z\"},{\"title\":\"What State Street Tech Select SPDR (XLK) Sold: Apple Leads on Nov. 9\",\"summary\":\"On Nov. 9 State Street’s Technology Select Sector SPDR (XLK) was the lone ETF tracked that day to sell, recording $136.7 million in gross ETF activity (all sell-side) for a net outflow of $136.7 million and trimming all 76 of its positions with no new buys or full exits. Its largest reductions were Apple (63,680 shares, −$22.3M, now 16.34% of the fund), Nvidia (105,584 shares, −$18.9M, 13.80%), and Microsoft (32,400 shares, −$17.7M, 12.92%); Broadcom and AMD each saw about $6.6M trimmed. XLK holds 76 large-cap tech stocks (100% large cap), with 65.1% of assets in its top 10 positions, an expense ratio of 0.08%, GF Score 90, P/E 32.31, P/B 10.93, dividend yield 0.52% and a year-to-date return of +17.75%. Watch for whether future updates show continued broad cuts or a return to adding to its largest tech names.\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/state-street-tech-select-spdr-110443420.html\",\"article_id\":\"367e6e9d-6fdb-30fa-a189-2105374c281c\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:04:43Z\"},{\"title\":\"SPDR S&P 500 ETF (SPY) Adds Apple and Nvidia on Monday\",\"summary\":\"On Nov. 9, 2026 SPDR S&P 500 ETF Trust (SPY) bought $4.32 billion of stock and sold nothing, increasing all 503 of its positions and producing a net inflow into its holdings; the $791.88 billion fund’s largest purchases were Apple (969,795 shares, $340.1M, now 7.87% of the fund), Nvidia (1,608,160 shares, $287.3M, 6.64%), and Microsoft (493,465 shares, $269.0M, 6.22%), followed by Amazon ($174.1M) and Alphabet ($112.4M). SPY holds 503 stocks with 37.4% of assets in its top 10, is heavily weighted to Technology (36.9%), charges a 0.09% expense ratio, and shows a GF Score of 88, P/E 19.33, P/B 4.37, dividend yield 1.01% and year-to-date return of 10.83%.\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/spdr-p-500-etf-spy-110306154.html\",\"article_id\":\"0aa32bf3-cd5f-31f2-aac1-35ff4f882222\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:03:06Z\"},{\"title\":\"Invesco QQQ Trust (QQQ) Buys $206.7 Million More Apple on Nov. 9\",\"summary\":\"On Nov. 9, 2026 INVESCO QQQ Trust (QQQ) made a one-sided move, buying $2.44 billion of stock and selling nothing — increasing all 101 of its positions — while managing $463.70 billion in assets. Its biggest purchases were Apple ($206.7 million, now 8.47% of the fund), NVIDIA ($173.9 million, 7.13%), Microsoft ($163.5 million, 6.70%), Amazon ($116.3 million, 4.76%) and AMD ($92.6 million, 3.79%). QQQ is an all–large-cap equity ETF with 46.7% of assets in its top 10 holdings, heavy exposure to Technology (55.6%), Communication Services (11.9%) and Consumer Cyclical (11.7%), an expense ratio of 0.18%, a GF Score of 89, P/E of 22.8, P/B of 7.02, dividend yield of 0.45% and a year-to-date return of 10.21%. Investors should watch whether future updates continue broad accumulation or begin trimming the largest weights such as Apple.\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/invesco-qqq-trust-qqq-buys-110316461.html\",\"article_id\":\"e88ec31f-8052-3c36-b62f-cf88c53ae3d5\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:03:16Z\"},{\"title\":\"What ProShares Ultra S&P500 2x Shares (SSO) Sold: Apple Leads on Monday\",\"summary\":\"ProShares Ultra S&P500 2x Shares (SSO) sold $191.9 million of stocks on Monday — the fund made no purchases and trimmed 498 positions, producing a net outflow of $191.9 million from $7.02 billion in assets. Its biggest sales were Apple ($15.1M, leaving a 7.86% weight), NVIDIA ($12.8M, 6.64% weight) and Microsoft ($12.0M, 6.22% weight); smaller trims included Amazon and Alphabet. SSO is a 2x leveraged equity ETF holding 502 stocks, with the top 10 holdings at 37.3% of assets, large caps 99.9%, and heavy exposure to technology (36.8%), financials (12.3%) and healthcare (10.5%). Key fund metrics: expense ratio 0.88%, GF Score 88, P/E 23.15, P/B 4.73, dividend yield 0.71%, and year-to-date return +15.25%. Investors should watch whether future updates continue broad reductions or shift back to adding exposure.\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/proshares-ultra-p500-2x-shares-110428472.html\",\"article_id\":\"84361151-514b-3152-b508-b001edc1bc70\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:04:28Z\"},{\"title\":\"Proshares Trust (TQQQ) Buys $70.7 Million More Apple on Nov. 9\",\"summary\":\"On Nov. 9, 2026 ProShares UltraPro QQQ (TQQQ) reported one-sided trading: it increased every one of its 100 positions, recording $830.5 million in gross (and net) purchases with no sales. Its largest buys were Apple ($70.7M, 201,582 shares, 8.51% of the fund), NVIDIA ($59.5M, 7.16%), Microsoft ($55.9M, 6.73%), Amazon ($39.8M, 4.79%) and AMD ($31.7M, 3.81%). TQQQ is a 3x leveraged alternative equity fund with a 0.94% expense ratio, 100% large-cap holdings, heavy tech exposure (55.8%), top-10 concentration of 46.9%, a GF Score of 88, P/E 28.19, P/B 7.24, 1.1% dividend yield and a year-to-date return of +7.92%. Investors should watch whether the fund continues to add across all positions or starts trimming, which would end the current streak.\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/proshares-trust-tqqq-buys-70-110328180.html\",\"article_id\":\"acc361ec-e2b8-3982-9462-2f71dacd7d2c\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:03:28Z\"},{\"title\":\"iShares Core S&P 500 (IVV) Sells $17.8 Million More Apple on Monday\",\"summary\":\"On Nov. 9, iShares Core S&P 500 ETF (IVV) reported $235.6 million in gross trading against $871.72 billion in assets and was a net seller of $216.2 million—reducing 497 positions and increasing just one. Its largest trim was a $17.8 million sale of Apple, with other top sells including NVIDIA ($15.1M), Microsoft ($14.1M), Amazon ($9.1M) and Alphabet A ($5.9M). The single notable buy was Allstate (+$9.7M, 0.10% of the fund); no new positions were opened and none were fully exited. IVV holds 503 stocks, with its top 10 making up 37.4% of assets, technology the biggest sector (36.9%), an expense ratio of 0.03%, and top weights in AAPL (7.87%), NVDA (6.65%), MSFT (6.22%), AMZN (4.03%) and GOOGL (2.60%). The article suggests watching for further trims of mega-cap names or a shift back to net buying, and whether Allstate’s stake grows beyond 0.1%.\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ishares-core-p-500-ivv-110414054.html\",\"article_id\":\"7798470d-671e-38a9-ba7c-633849de29be\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:04:14Z\"},{\"title\":\"Invesco NASDAQ 100 ETF (QQQM) Buys $35.0 Million More Apple on Monday\",\"summary\":\"On Nov. 9, 2026 Invesco NASDAQ 100 ETF (QQQM) — a $106.99 billion fund — bought $413.0 million of stock, increasing every one of its 101 holdings with no sells, exits or new positions. Its largest purchases were Apple ($35.0M, 99,752 shares, 8.47% of the fund), NVIDIA ($29.4M, 164,724 shares, 7.13%), Microsoft ($27.7M, 50,764 shares, 6.70%), Amazon ($19.7M) and AMD ($15.7M). QQQM is concentrated in large-cap tech (55.6% of classified holdings), with the top 10 holdings making up 46.7% of assets; it has an expense ratio of 0.15%, a GF Score of 88, P/E of 28.82, dividend yield of 0.45% and a year-to-date return of 10.26%. Investors should watch whether the fund continues broad-based buying or begins trimming positions in future updates.\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/invesco-nasdaq-100-etf-qqqm-110351078.html\",\"article_id\":\"4f6df130-db42-3bcc-9dab-2f9ee5f50556\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:03:51Z\"},{\"title\":\"55 ETFs Add to Apple (AAPL) Holdings on Nov. 9\",\"summary\":\"On Nov. 9, 2026, 55 ETFs increased their Apple (AAPL) holdings while 20 cut them, resulting in net ETF buying of $716.3 million and leaving 193 funds unchanged. The largest buyers by dollar value were SPY ($340.1M, +969,795 shares), QQQ ($206.7M, +589,392 shares) and SPYM ($75.6M), with leveraged/other ETFs such as TQQQ and QQQM also adding exposure. Over the last five reported days ETFs were net buyers on three days and sellers on two, making the recent trend mostly buying and marking a two-day buying streak following net outflows on Nov. 4–5. Apple, in the Technology/Consumer Electronics sector, has a $5.06 trillion market cap, trailing-12-month revenue of $478.83 billion (+17.3% year over year), gross margin 48.8% and net margin 27.6%. Its valuation metrics include P/E 38.83, P/B 45.18, P/S 10.72; GF Score 94 with a GF Value of $298.33 versus a price of $348.51, dividend yield 0.34% and year-to-date return +28.54%. Investors should watch whether ETF flows continue the buying trend.\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/55-etfs-add-apple-aapl-110045108.html\",\"article_id\":\"5ace43f3-2823-3f0e-9e35-e6b81bcd5c24\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:00:45Z\"},{\"title\":\"Is Seagate A Better Way Than Apple To Own AI Hardware Demand?\",\"summary\":\"The article compares Apple and Seagate as ways to play AI-driven hardware demand, arguing Seagate is the more direct bet because data-center customers took 90% of capacity in the September quarter and have long-term supply agreements through calendar 2028 that allocate the vast majority of Seagate’s available capacity. Seagate expects December-quarter revenue of about $4.8 billion (±$100M) after $4.2 billion in September, reported a fiscal Q1 2027 operating margin of 48.9% (vs. 26.9% a year earlier), plans capital spending of 4–6% of revenue, and expects to hold more cash than debt by end-2026; 2028 prices have not yet been set. Apple, by contrast, gave only a one-quarter outlook (December revenue growth 7–10% after 12% in September) and is supply-constrained on memory, which pressured gross margin (47.9% in September, forecast 45–46% in December). On trailing-12-month measures Seagate is cheaper, faster-growing and more profitable (P/E 26.3 vs. Apple 38.7; revenue growth 44.4% vs. 15.1%; operating margin 40.5% vs. 33.0%), though Apple carries slightly less debt relative to market value (1.6% vs. Seagate’s 2.3%) and previously sustained higher margins. The article cautions that Seagate’s pricing — and its ability to keep margins high when 2028 prices are set — is the key risk, and Seagate’s next margin report (expected January 2027) will be important to watch.\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://www.trefis.com/stock/aapl/articles/623932/is-seagate-a-better-way-than-apple-to-own-ai-hardware-demand/2026-11-10\",\"article_id\":\"b88491e5-639e-31df-b454-9df7c18349fa\",\"provider_url\":\"https://www.trefis.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"Trefis\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"https://media.zenfs.com/en/trefis_142/e105eb3be0bf5179099a86144d95cb2a.png\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T01:50:49Z\"}],\"beta\":1.089,\"sector\":\"Technology\",\"industry\":\"Consumer Electronics\",\"stock_ticker\":\"AAPL\",\"market_benchmark_ticker\":\"SPX\",\"sector_benchmark_ticker\":\"XLK\",\"SPX_percentage_price_change\":0.88,\"recent_insider_transactions\":null,\"stock_percentage_price_change\":-0.75,\"sector_percentage_price_change\":2.6,\"recent_analyst_upgrades_summary\":null},\"debug\":{},\"query\":\"Explain the price movement in AAPL today\",\"ticker\":\"AAPL\",\"explanation\":{\"tldr\":\"Apple (AAPL) fell 0.75% as ETF trading was mixed, with broad funds adding to the name while some tech vehicles trimmed it, even as Technology rose 2.6% and the SPX gained 0.88%.\",\"short_tldr\":\"mixed ETF flows are shaping sentiment.\",\"bottom_line\":\"Apple’s dip looks tied to a tug of war in ETF positioning, not a weak market backdrop.\",\"observations\":{\"ETF flows\":\"Multiple funds added Apple, including SPY, QQQ, and QQQM, and the group of ETFs showed net buying of $716.3 million over the last five reported days. But several tech and leveraged funds also sold it, including XLK and IVV.\",\"Beta context\":\"Beta is 1.089, so Apple moved roughly in line with the market rather than acting like a high-octane growth name.\",\"Market context\":\"The broader market was firm, but Apple still slipped while some ETF holders rotated exposure, showing the stock did not fully participate in the sector rally.\",\"Relative strength\":\"Apple lagged the Technology sector, which rose 2.6%, and also underperformed the 0.88% gain in the SPX. That points to pressure specific to the stock versus the broader tape.\"}},\"show_insight\":false,\"trace_id\":\"32db69f0-ae41-4102-a1db-6661864478a7\",\"id\":\"32db69f0-ae41-4102-a1db-6661864478a7\",\"symbol_id\":\"753c0cb0-a9d9-4765-9a03-51574991381d\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-11T11:38:48.682052+00:00\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-11T11:38:48.682052+00:00\",\"dynamic_questions\":[]},\"news_summary\":{\"debug\":{},\"limit\":20,\"quote\":{\"session\":\"pre_market\",\"quote_type\":\"EQUITY\",\"price_basis\":\"fullday\",\"market_state\":\"PRE\",\"prompt_basis\":\"fullday\",\"prompt_dropped\":null,\"resolved_price\":346.4883,\"pct_generated_at\":\"2026-11-11T11:45:49.263066+00:00\",\"regular_market_price\":348.51,\"stale_fullday_change\":false,\"prompt_change_percent\":-0.58009756,\"fullday_change_percent\":-0.58009756,\"resolved_change_percent\":-0.58009756,\"regular_market_change_percent\":-0.62163},\"min_score\":0.1,\"fund_facts\":null,\"news_summary\":{\"id\":\"AAPL\",\"tldr\":\"Apple was the subject of substantial ETF activity on November 9, with **55 funds adding shares** and aggregate ETF buying of **$716.3 million**. The flows were mixed across funds, while a separate comparison highlighted Apple’s memory-supply pressure and slower near-term outlook versus Seagate.\",\"themes\":[{\"theme_name\":\"Broad ETF Demand\",\"theme_description\":\"Large index and technology-focused funds produced strong net buying. ETF means exchange-traded fund, a basket of securities traded like a stock.\"},{\"theme_name\":\"Mixed Fund Positioning\",\"theme_description\":\"Buying was concentrated in broad-market and Nasdaq funds. XLK, IVV, and SSO reduced Apple exposure during the same session.\"},{\"theme_name\":\"Memory Supply Pressure\",\"theme_description\":\"The Trefis comparison said Apple faces memory constraints that could pressure its December-quarter gross margin.\"},{\"theme_name\":\"Premium Valuation\",\"theme_description\":\"The coverage reported Apple trading at roughly **38.8 times trailing earnings**, meaning investors pay a high price relative to recent per-share profit.\"}],\"summary\":\"Apple’s ETF flows were positive overall on November 9. SPY, QQQ, SPYM, TQQQ, and QQQM added shares, while XLK, IVV, and SSO reduced exposure. The largest reported purchase came from SPY at **$340.1 million**. The largest reported sale came from XLK at approximately **$22.3 million**. Apple’s authoritative move is **down 0.58% in today’s pre-market move against the prior close**; the regular session has not opened. A separate analysis compared Apple with Seagate for AI-hardware exposure. It described Apple’s December revenue outlook as **7% to 10% growth**, following **12% growth** in September, and cited expected December gross margin of **45% to 46%** versus **47.9%** in September. The comparison identified memory availability and margin pressure as key Apple issues.\",\"key_events\":[\"ETF Buying Activity (November 9, 2026): **55 ETFs increased Apple holdings**, while 20 reduced positions, producing reported net ETF buying of **$716.3 million**.\",\"Major Index Fund Purchases (November 9, 2026): SPY added **$340.1 million** of Apple, QQQ added **$206.7 million**, and SPYM added **$75.6 million**.\",\"Technology ETF Reduction (November 9, 2026): XLK reduced Apple by **63,680 shares**, worth approximately **$22.3 million**, while trimming every holding.\",\"Leveraged ETF Activity (November 9, 2026): TQQQ added **$70.7 million** of Apple, while SSO sold approximately **$15.1 million**.\"],\"dynamic_sections\":[{\"section_title\":\"ETF Flows\",\"section_content\":\"Broad-market funds drove the strongest buying. SPY purchased **969,795 Apple shares**, while QQQ purchased **589,392 shares**. These flows increased Apple’s reported fund weights to **7.87% in SPY** and **8.47% in QQQ**.\"},{\"section_title\":\"Contrasting Fund Decisions\",\"section_content\":\"XLK reduced Apple by **63,680 shares**, and IVV sold approximately **$17.8 million** of Apple. These sales contrasted with broad buying from SPY, QQQ, SPYM, QQQM, and TQQQ.\"},{\"section_title\":\"Business Outlook\",\"section_content\":\"The coverage described Apple’s December-quarter outlook as slower than its September-quarter growth. It also cited memory constraints as a potential gross-margin pressure.\"},{\"section_title\":\"Valuation And Risks\",\"section_content\":\"The article reported Apple’s trailing price-to-earnings ratio at approximately **38.8** and its market capitalization at **$5.06 trillion**. Key risks include premium valuation, memory availability, and weaker margin performance.\"}]},\"articles_info\":[{\"about\":[\"AAPL\"],\"title\":\"State Street SPDR Portfolio S&P 500 (SPYM) Buys $75.6 Million More Apple on Monday\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/state-street-spdr-portfolio-p-110320237.html\",\"article_id\":\"a612223c-75f9-3325-babd-1f086b72d615\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:03:20Z\"},{\"about\":[\"AAPL\"],\"title\":\"What State Street Tech Select SPDR (XLK) Sold: Apple Leads on Nov. 9\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/state-street-tech-select-spdr-110443420.html\",\"article_id\":\"367e6e9d-6fdb-30fa-a189-2105374c281c\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:04:43Z\"},{\"about\":[\"AAPL\"],\"title\":\"SPDR S&P 500 ETF (SPY) Adds Apple and Nvidia on Monday\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/spdr-p-500-etf-spy-110306154.html\",\"article_id\":\"0aa32bf3-cd5f-31f2-aac1-35ff4f882222\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:03:06Z\"},{\"about\":[\"AAPL\"],\"title\":\"Invesco QQQ Trust (QQQ) Buys $206.7 Million More Apple on Nov. 9\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/invesco-qqq-trust-qqq-buys-110316461.html\",\"article_id\":\"e88ec31f-8052-3c36-b62f-cf88c53ae3d5\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:03:16Z\"},{\"about\":[\"AAPL\"],\"title\":\"What ProShares Ultra S&P500 2x Shares (SSO) Sold: Apple Leads on Monday\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/proshares-ultra-p500-2x-shares-110428472.html\",\"article_id\":\"84361151-514b-3152-b508-b001edc1bc70\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:04:28Z\"},{\"about\":[\"AAPL\"],\"title\":\"Proshares Trust (TQQQ) Buys $70.7 Million More Apple on Nov. 9\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/proshares-trust-tqqq-buys-70-110328180.html\",\"article_id\":\"acc361ec-e2b8-3982-9462-2f71dacd7d2c\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:03:28Z\"},{\"about\":[\"AAPL\"],\"title\":\"iShares Core S&P 500 (IVV) Sells $17.8 Million More Apple on Monday\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/ishares-core-p-500-ivv-110414054.html\",\"article_id\":\"7798470d-671e-38a9-ba7c-633849de29be\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:04:14Z\"},{\"about\":[\"AAPL\"],\"title\":\"Invesco NASDAQ 100 ETF (QQQM) Buys $35.0 Million More Apple on Monday\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/invesco-nasdaq-100-etf-qqqm-110351078.html\",\"article_id\":\"4f6df130-db42-3bcc-9dab-2f9ee5f50556\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:03:51Z\"},{\"about\":[\"AAPL\"],\"title\":\"55 ETFs Add to Apple (AAPL) Holdings on Nov. 9\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/55-etfs-add-apple-aapl-110045108.html\",\"article_id\":\"5ace43f3-2823-3f0e-9e35-e6b81bcd5c24\",\"provider_url\":\"http://www.gurufocus.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"GuruFocus.com\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T11:00:45Z\"},{\"about\":[\"AAPL\"],\"title\":\"Is Seagate A Better Way Than Apple To Own AI Hardware Demand?\",\"yahoo_url\":\"https://www.trefis.com/stock/aapl/articles/623932/is-seagate-a-better-way-than-apple-to-own-ai-hardware-demand/2026-11-10\",\"article_id\":\"b88491e5-639e-31df-b454-9df7c18349fa\",\"provider_url\":\"https://www.trefis.com/\",\"provider_name\":\"Trefis\",\"thumbnail_url\":\"https://media.zenfs.com/en/trefis_142/e105eb3be0bf5179099a86144d95cb2a.png\",\"published_date\":\"2026-11-11T01:50:49Z\"}],\"compliance_check\":null,\"inherited_news_from\":[],\"generation_start_time\":\"2026-11-11T11: